{"status":"success","type":"premium_reasoning","answer":"**Core Insight**  \nRFC 8785 defines the JSON Canonicalization Scheme (JCS): a deterministic way to serialize equivalent JSON data identically.\n\n**Key Analysis**  \nIt is used before cryptographic hashing, signing, or verification so semantically identical JSON produces the same bytes; it standardizes property ordering, number formatting, and escaping, but does not provide encryption or authenticity itself.\n\n**Key Assumptions**  \n- Inputs conform to JCS-compatible JSON/I-JSON constraints  \n- All participants implement RFC 8785 identically  \n- Non-conforming values or differing serialization rules invalidate signatures\n\n**Recommended Action**  \nUse RFC 8785 when JSON must be signed, hashed, or compared across systems, and canonicalize before—not after—cryptographic processing.","related":[{"resource":"https://api.babyblueviper.com/review","description":"invinoveritas /review — a signed neutral verdict BEFORE an irreversible action, committed before the outcome it's graded against. Recomputable from public data, no TEE, no trusted scorer. Pre-trade risk check, code revie","payment":"same x402 flow as this call (402 challenge at the URL), or Bearer credits"},{"resource":"https://api.babyblueviper.com/decision","description":"invinoveritas /decision — structured decisions with confidence + risk scoring that ship with a SIGNED PROVENANCE PROOF: recompute offline to confirm invinoveritas issued this exact verdict untampered (provenance, not a c","payment":"same x402 flow as this call (402 challenge at the URL), or Bearer credits"},{"resource":"https://api.babyblueviper.com/execute","description":"invinoveritas /execute — sandboxed Python that returns a SIGNED PROVENANCE PROOF of the exact output you recompute offline to confirm the run is untampered. Hardened Docker (network off, read-only root, caps dropped, non","payment":"same x402 flow as this call (402 challenge at the URL), or Bearer credits"},{"reso